What is derived, and Changes made to it
---------------------------------------

1. layouts/ormus.json is Herdr's `main` layout, cloned (its mod.json marker
   says cloned_from main 0.1.15). Changes: the theme, fonts, 14 px pane
   corners, the sidebar blocks (the Ormus header, Needs you / Overview, the
   Flock sidebar), and the pane header mod.
2. mods/ormus-chrome/main.js is Herdr's `workspace-chrome` mod, cloned.
   Changes: the Ormus mark and wordmark in the sidebar header, the search
   button opens the Ormus picker, the Settings and Add machine rows.
3. mods/ormus-spaces, mods/ormus-picker and mods/ormus-pane are NOT in this
   repo. The install builds them in your Herdr home from your own copies of
   Herdr's `spaces`, `picker` and `pane` mods, with anchored edits
   (src/space_tiles.py and src/pane_head.py). The anchors are the few lines of
   Herdr's code, copied from 0.1.15, that the edits look for. Changes: a logo
   or accent tile per space, a name per pane, a Spotlight button, an Overview
   window.
4. themes/*.json follow the theme format of Herdr and carry its color names;
   the colors are the Ormus palette.
5. The icons in mods/ormus-chrome/*.svg (except ormus-mark.svg) are Lucide
   icons (https://lucide.dev, ISC license; parts from Feather, MIT license,
   Copyright (c) 2013-2022 Cole Bemis). Both license texts are in
   LICENSE-LUCIDE.txt.
6. The Ormus mark (mods/ormus-chrome/ormus-mark.svg, examples/logos/
   ormus-mark.svg) and the wordmark are the Ormus brand's. The MIT license of
   this repo does not give the right to use them as another brand.

Each modified file that can carry a comment says so at its top: mods/ormus-chrome/main.js,
and the three mods the install builds (a header line is added to each).

Everything else (mods/ormus-needs, mods/ormus-search, mods/ormus-cards, the
install tool) is written for this repo and uses only the mod API of Herdr.
Its Needs you view and Overview borrow ideas from Flockbook
(https://github.com/minchenlee/flockbook, MIT license); the code is new.

Fonts: Inter (Copyright 2016 The Inter Project Authors, the line in the font's own name table) and Cormorant Garamond (Copyright 2015 The Cormorant Project Authors) are under the SIL Open Font License 1.1.
Their notices are next to the font files (mods/ormus-chrome/fonts/*-OFL.txt)
